# EOD — daily work log + Geekbot standup

**Gather everything I touched, write it down, then file the standup.** One command at
the end of the workday: sweep every work tool, consolidate into the notes file
(backfilling any days I forgot), then walk the Geekbot standup questions and post them.

Run this at Ahmed's desk — the Geekbot phase is interactive (prompt-and-wait), so it
cannot be a headless cron. A companion headless task `eod-prefetch` runs at 20:00
Sun–Thu and drops a draft at `~/.claude/eod-drafts/eod-<YYYY-MM-DD>.md` so this skill is
fast; if that draft exists, start from it, but still fill the gaps it couldn't reach.

`--dry-run`: do Phases 0–2 compose + preview only — no notes write, no Geekbot send.

