## Phase 0 — Window & inputs

1. `head -1` the notes file → last logged date (top `# YYYY-MM-DD`). Window =
   (last-logged + 1) … today.
2. If `~/.claude/eod-drafts/eod-<today>.md` exists, read it as the starting draft (it
   covers git + GitHub reliably; MCP sources may be marked pending).
3. State the window to the user before gathering.

## Phase 1 — Gather (fill every source for the window)

Load the MCP tools you'll need in ONE `ToolSearch` call. For each source not already
covered by the draft, query the whole window.

- **Local git** (authoritative for commits) — per repo and worktree:
  ```bash
  for d in "" cashflow-api cashflow-console cashflow-e2e wt-*; do
    p="{{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/Code/foodics/cashflow/$d"
    git -C "$p" log --author="Ahmed Shahwan" --since="<from> 00:00" --until="<to> 23:59" \
        --pretty=format:'%ad %h %s' --date=short 2>/dev/null
    git -C "$p" status -sb 2>/dev/null | head -3
    git -C "$p" log --branches --not --remotes --author="Ahmed Shahwan" \
        --pretty=format:'unpushed: %ad %h %s' --date=short 2>/dev/null   # WIP
  done
  ```
- **GitHub** (`export GH_HOST=github.foodics.com`):
  ```bash
  gh search prs   --author=@me      --json number,title,repository,state,updatedAt,url "updated:>=<from>"
  gh search prs   --reviewed-by=@me --json number,title,repository,state,updatedAt,url "updated:>=<from>"
  gh search prs   --involves=@me    --json number,title,repository,state,updatedAt,url "updated:>=<from>"
  ```
  Per-PR detail if needed: `gh api repos/pay/<repo>/pulls/<N>/reviews` and `/comments`.
- **Jira** — `searchJiraIssuesUsingJql`, cloudId `foodics-products.atlassian.net`:
  `(assignee = currentUser() OR worklogAuthor = currentUser()) AND updated >= "<from>" ORDER BY updated DESC`,
  `fields: [summary,status,issuetype,updated]`. If the result is too large to inline, it's
  saved to a file — `jq -r '.issues.nodes[] | "\(.key)\t\(.fields.status.name)\t\(.fields.updated[0:10])\t\(.fields.summary)"'` it.
- **Confluence** — `searchConfluenceUsingCql`: `contributor = currentUser() and lastmodified >= "<from>" ORDER BY lastmodified DESC` (filter to `type=page` unless attachments matter).
- **Slack** — his messages in the window (search `from:@me` date-scoped).
- **Gmail** — `search_threads` `from:me after:<from>` (mostly calendar accepts/declines — mine for meeting signal, not real correspondence).
- **Calendar** — `list_events` for the window → the `Meetings` group.
- **Drive** — `list_recent_files` / `search_files` → docs touched (link inline).

If a connector errors or is absent, note it as a coverage gap; never fail the whole run.

## Phase 2 — Consolidate & write notes

Consolidate, **deduplicate** (one unit of work = one bullet; a commit + its PR + its Jira
issue are the same unit — prefer the richest link), **expurgate** noise, **refine** to the
compact recent style (~8–20 lines/day). Bucket by **author date** of the commit / merge /
status change.

- One `# YYYY-MM-DD` block per active day, **newest-first**.
- `- [x]` merged/done, `- [ ]` open/in-flight; informal group labels seen in the file:
  `Merged — <repo>`, `My open PRs — follow-up`, `PR Reviews — peers`, `Tickets follow-up`,
  `Docs`, `Meetings`, `WIP (unpushed)`, `Exploring:`, `AI review fixes — acted on my approval`.
- Links: Jira `https://foodics-products.atlassian.net/browse/EE-XXXX`; GitHub
  `https://github.foodics.com/pay/<repo>/pull/<n>`; append `— author/status` on peer-review lines.
- **Preview the full composed block(s) and wait for confirmation** before writing (it's
  his long-lived notes). Call out any judgment calls (weekend days, inferred PR numbers,
  AI-fix PRs).
- `--dry-run` **stops here**: show the preview, then no write, no draft deletion, no Geekbot.
- On approval, **prepend** at the very top of the file (anchor-edit before the current top
  `# <last-logged>` heading, with a `---` separator between). Then delete the consumed draft.

## Phase 3 — Geekbot standup (interactive)

1. Read the Geekbot DM (`slack_read_channel` on `D09RSDJTYFL`, ~30 msgs). Find the **3
   current questions** and **his last actual submission date** (a message from
   `Ahmed Shahwan`, not Geekbot's echo). Geekbot anchors "since <date>" to that last
   submission — which may be **weeks** before the last notes date, so scope Q1 to it.
2. Ask **one question at a time, waiting for each answer**:
   - **Q1 — "What have you done since <date>?"** Pre-fill a themed draft synthesized from
     the notes (read the file across the whole "since" span, not just today). Group by
     epic/theme (SADAD, Modular Monolith, VIBAN/SNB, E2E suite, AI tooling, Reviews). User edits/confirms.
   - **Q2 — "What will you do tomorrow?"** Propose from his open PRs + in-progress/code-review
     Jira + upcoming calendar. Note OOO days (a declined standup invite = OOO). User confirms.
   - **Q3 — "Anything blocking your progress?"** Ask; default `No blockers.` if none.
3. **Post each answer as its own message** to the DM (Geekbot advances one question per
   message). After each send, re-read the DM to confirm Geekbot posted the next question
   before sending the next answer. Sending on his behalf → he confirmed each answer above,
   which is the go-ahead.
   - **Formatting:** use `**bold**` (double asterisk) for section headers — single `*` renders
     as italic through the Slack MCP. Bullets `•` and nested `◦` match his house report style.
4. Confirm Geekbot's closing "Awesome, thank you!" and report the message links.

## Out of Scope

- Creating commits/PRs, editing tickets, transitioning Jira, or replying in team channels.
- Auto-sending Geekbot answers without per-answer confirmation.
- Writing the notes file without showing the preview first.
- The headless gather — that's `eod-prefetch` (see `~/.claude/scheduled-tasks/eod-prefetch/`).
